<title>FINLAND: SANTASALO, TAMFELT GET GOVT FUNDS.</title>
<headline>SANTASALO, TAMFELT GET GOVT FUNDS.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish engineering group Santasalo-JOT Oy and forming fabrics marker Tamfelt Oy have been granted government investment support funds designed to boost job creation, the Labour Ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>Santasalo was granted six million markka and Tamfelt received 2.2 million, the ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>The grant to Santasalo was made for investments at Karkkila where it is expected to create 65 jobs, the ministry said.</p>
<p>The support to Tamfelt was earmarked for investments at Juankoski, where it was expected to create 30 jobs, it said.</p>
<p>The grants to the two groups was part of more than 13 million markka in investment support granted to firms by the Labour Ministry, it said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 235</p>
</text>
